meta {
  name: list-low-ratings
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/admin/v1/reviews?max_rating=3
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  max_rating: 3
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

tests {
  test("responds 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200)
  })

  test("returns nothing above the ceiling", function () {
    // The seeded run leaves a single 4-star review, so this list is legitimately empty. The
    // assertion is on the FILTER holding, not on there being rows -- a test that needed rows
    // would fail on a clean database for a reason unrelated to the filter.
    const above = res.body.data.reviews.filter((r) => r.rating > 3)
    expect(above).to.have.length(0)
  })
}

docs {
  # The complaints

`max_rating=3` is the query this screen exists for. A manager opens the reviews page mid-service to
find out which table is unhappy while there is still time to walk over to it.

Pair with `has_comment=true` when you want only the ones somebody explained.
}
